  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 355 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nNorth to northwest flow prevails through the weekend and into \nMonday, with a weak shortwave expected to move through the area \nSaturday. Scattered precipitation will accompany this wave, with\nwintry mix or snow expected, mainly along and north of Highway \n200. Northwest winds increase during the late morning and \nafternoon, with gusts up to 30 mph. The combination of falling \nsnow and gusty northwest winds could bring brief periodic \nvisibility reductions. This will depend on the intensity of \npotential heavier snow showers, with the highest probability \nbeing in the northern Red River Valley and northwest Minnesota. \n\nA surge of cold air follows the shortwave, with highs in the \n20s Sunday afternoon and lows falling into the teens Sunday \nnight. H5 flow turns nearly zonal by Tuesday, allowing \ntemperatures to climb into the 30s and low 40s through the \nremainder of next week.",
